	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["7AF6FD3F4F3B06B4"]
			description: [
				"From the far side of the Moon, the antenna can just make out Mercury in the Sun's glare and Venus under its clouds, and you're going to both. First, though, the atom: uranium from the End, a hot cell and a reactor that burns nothing."
				"IV hatches wait for Mercury's iridium, and until then two EV energy hatches run any IV multiblock."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:iv_machine_hull"
			id: "3FB9EA4152DCD1D3"
			rewards: [{ id: "7044ED917D669557", type: "xp", xp: 50 }]
			shape: "rsquare"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [{ id: "57DEFEB8476D0C21", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Inner Planets"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3FB9EA4152DCD1D3"]
			description: [
				"There's a new Overworld vein of fluorite, barite, galena and sphalerite, and it only grows in freshly generated chunks. Time to go somewhere you've never been."
				"Raw fluorite and raw barite make a &6Fluorite Vein Sample&r, and any vein drill takes it, steam ones included."
			]
			icon: "grindless:vein_sample_fluorite"
			id: "5C008907C9055459"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "7B9F1E328EB5EE2F", type: "xp", xp: 40 }
				{ count: 8, id: "3F7CDDC11E9E812C", item: "gcyr:raw_fluorite", type: "item" }
			]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5E187BE14C983E81", item: "grindless:vein_sample_fluorite", type: "item" }
				{ count: 16L, id: "77F69ECE1ABFC4AE", item: "gcyr:raw_fluorite", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Fluorite Vein"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5C008907C9055459"]
			description: [
				"Fluorite and sulfuric acid go in at the cold end of the &6Fluorspar Kiln&r, and hydrofluoric acid comes out of the scrubber at the hot one. That's the fluorine for enrichment, and nobody grinds a mountain of mica for it."
				"It runs lots of charges at once instead of overclocking, and its gypsum goes into concrete."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:fluorspar_kiln"
			id: "5EE3EB2547415591"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "51B3F0619D171EC0", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 6, id: "794706880191B58A", item: "gcyr:fluorite_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "15DE13E4D77E3653", item: "gtceu:fluorspar_kiln", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3CF6C2C31D340263", item: "gtceu:hydrofluoric_acid_bucket", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Fluorspar Kiln"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3FB9EA4152DCD1D3"]
			description: [
				"The End's pitchblende vein has been there all along, and no drill will touch it: you're going to dissolve the uranium right out of the rock."
				"Its raw pitchblende and raw uraninite make an &6End Pitchblende Vein Sample&r."
			]
			icon: "grindless:vein_sample_pitchblende_end"
			id: "77B6F588980A4B1C"
			rewards: [{ id: "70655102B05149BB", type: "xp", xp: 40 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7D0E205645D080F6", item: "grindless:vein_sample_pitchblende_end", type: "item" }]
			title: "Pitchblende"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77B6F588980A4B1C"]
			description: [
				"Four wells push acid into the rock, one pulls the uranium back up, and resin in the header house catches it. The &6In-Situ Leach Field&r only works in the End, and you do dig the five wells yourself."
				"The sample is never used up, the resin wears slowly, and the odd bit of radioactive waste goes into storage, not a chest by the door."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:isr_wellfield"
			id: "5FD0B9548159D199"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "1845E73B52D4284A", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 2, id: "72A3FD84380B88BE", item: "grindless:ion_exchange_resin", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ count: 4L, id: "3F9C133862854E97", item: "grindless:ion_exchange_resin", type: "item" }
				{ id: "743B9F4AD256F24B", item: "gtceu:isr_wellfield", type: "item" }
				{ count: 30L, id: "7DAF0BEA5BE61AD0", item: "gtceu:uraninite_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "In-Situ Leach Field"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3FB9EA4152DCD1D3"]
			description: ["Both the hot cell and the reactor hide behind &6Radiation-Proof Machine Casing&r, lead-heavy blocks out of the IV assembler. They're set in concrete, and clay concrete does fine until the kiln's gypsum turns up."]
			icon: "gtnn:radiation_proof_machine_casing"
			id: "5BDF50007C1EAFE2"
			rewards: [{ id: "7503D049BFB5C02C", type: "xp", xp: 40 }]
			tasks: [{ count: 54L, id: "70F4496C01D4AED9", item: "gtnn:radiation_proof_machine_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Radiation-Proof Casing"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5BDF50007C1EAFE2"]
			description: ["The &6Hot Cell&r is where uranium stops being something you carry around. It rides in and out on buses, the programmed circuit picks the job, and the tongs behind the lead-glass windows do the touching."]
			icon: "gtceu:hot_cell"
			id: "30D78F6EB49AF27B"
			rewards: [{ id: "5FE2E31B75F05904", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "3E606383198DBAB6", item: "gtceu:hot_cell", type: "item" }]
			title: "Hot Cell"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30D78F6EB49AF27B", "5EE3EB2547415591", "5FD0B9548159D199"]
			description: [
				"Circuit 1 turns uraninite and hydrofluoric acid into &6Uranium 235&r and a pile of uranium 238. Keep the 238: the pellets, the radon and later MOX all want it."
				"The hexafluoride never leaves the cell, and the fluorine comes back out as gas."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:uranium_235_dust"
			id: "174353B4F6C61A79"
			rewards: [{ id: "31A78D220008DAFC", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "54EE2919EBE407C9", item: "gtceu:uranium_235_dust", type: "item" }
				{ id: "77DB1A0B29910D9C", item: "gtceu:uranium_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Enrichment"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["174353B4F6C61A79", "73D14393C00DE14D"]
			description: [
				"Circuit 4 blows air over uranium 238 for radon, and unlike GregTech's own recipe it needs no plutonium. A Nether Star soaked in radon in the chemical bath becomes a &6Quantum Star&r, and an Ender Eye becomes the Quantum Eye that EV sensors, emitters and scanners have been waiting for."
				"That stack from the simulator's Withers finally has a job."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:quantum_star"
			id: "7136B78C360303F9"
			rewards: [{ id: "76D5B425BB45E0F2", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "796CE71547E2EE7D", item: "gtceu:radon_bucket", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5D7EAB9D77291432", item: "gtceu:quantum_eye", type: "item" }
				{ id: "34220B07D73EBF63", item: "gtceu:quantum_star", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Quantum Star"
			x: 8.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7136B78C360303F9", "72022B0ECDC3668B"]
			description: [
				"The &6Fission Reactor&r runs uranium in four channels, with water through the core and a turbine hall out front, and it burns nothing. If the water or the room for spent fuel runs out, it shuts down instead of melting."
				"Its controller wants an IV field generator: a Quantum Star and samarium wire from Mars, which only melts in a blast furnace with HSS-G coils."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:fission_reactor"
			id: "774234968F1BEB95"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "7191AFDE0ABC670A", type: "xp", xp: 150 }
				{ count: 16, id: "336827B61BB005C1", item: "gtceu:light_concrete", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5B8B6955385CCA84", item: "gtceu:iv_field_generator", type: "item" }
				{ id: "314CE8A31C2B2D45", item: "gtceu:fission_reactor", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Fission Reactor"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["174353B4F6C61A79"]
			description: [
				"Real nuclear fuel is pellets in metal tubes, pressed, sintered and sealed with helium. The &6Fuel Fabrication Plant&r does the whole line, and the circuit picks the step."
				"You'll build it around an IV assembler, so maybe make two of those."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:fuel_fabrication_plant"
			id: "77A25AB4BB859C79"
			rewards: [{ id: "1E5C7EB0C7637A72", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "135CC8040C8DB996", item: "gtceu:fuel_fabrication_plant", type: "item" }]
			title: "Fuel Fabrication Plant"
			x: 8.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77A25AB4BB859C79", "004525B795119B1B"]
			description: [
				"An &6LEU Fuel Assembly&r is enriched uranium pressed into pellets and sealed in Zircaloy tubes with a breath of helium. The zirconium comes from the End's zircon, with a pinch of tin."
				"The sintering wants hydrogen in a hatch, but it never uses any up."
			]
			icon: "grindless:leu_fuel_assembly"
			id: "77E9A2979A7161D3"
			rewards: [{ id: "54040CCC26849B75", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1DE73D3441521EAC", item: "grindless:leu_pellet", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1C78223D64859AE3", item: "grindless:zircaloy_cladding_tube", type: "item" }
				{ id: "15DCE7EEEBD913CC", item: "grindless:leu_fuel_assembly", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "LEU Fuel"
			x: 10.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["774234968F1BEB95", "77E9A2979A7161D3"]
			description: [
				"Load an LEU assembly with circuit 1, give it water, and the reactor wakes up. Each assembly in the bus runs another channel, up to four, as long as the dynamo hatches can carry them."
				"IV dynamo hatches need Mercury's iridium, and until then the &6EV 16A Dynamo Hatch&r is the biggest you can give it."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:ev_energy_output_hatch_16a"
			id: "72139ED6F4E46D37"
			rewards: [{ id: "165CFE01A1667E2A", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "372DFA502C128D18", item: "gtceu:ev_energy_output_hatch_16a", type: "item" }]
			title: "First Criticality"
			x: 12.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["72139ED6F4E46D37"]
			description: [
				"An assembly lasts a good long while, then comes out spent, still holding uranium and the plutonium it bred. The hot cell's circuit 3 dissolves it in nitric acid and hands back the uranium and the &6Plutonium&r."
				"The waste is glassed and kept, and the fumes go back to making nitric acid."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:plutonium_dust"
			id: "7E266AE6DB3351F7"
			rewards: [{ id: "55D892B85E698FA5", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5EF89FF57108D2FB", item: "grindless:spent_fuel_assembly", type: "item" }
				{ id: "72A355DB71F7B4F7", item: "gtceu:plutonium_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Reprocessing"
			x: 14.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E266AE6DB3351F7"]
			description: [
				"Plutonium and uranium 238 in Zircaloy tubes make a &6MOX Fuel Assembly&r, which the reactor burns in heavy water on circuit 3."
				"A breeder assembly on circuit 4 gives less power but hands back more plutonium than it took."
			]
			icon: "grindless:mox_fuel_assembly"
			id: "16CAD9CBBF3B46D9"
			optional: true
			rewards: [{ id: "3BAB6E4A8186641F", type: "xp", xp: 40 }]
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "5764F970966E4FAE", item: "grindless:mox_fuel_assembly", type: "item" }]
			title: "MOX Fuel"
			x: 16.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E266AE6DB3351F7"]
			description: ["Plutonium oxide sealed in platinum and rhodium foil stays warm all on its own. The hot cell's circuit 2 makes an &6RTG Pellet&r, about as close to a pocket sun as GregTech will let you get."]
			icon: "grindless:rtg_pellet"
			id: "1D931CB1451E8B5A"
			rewards: [{ id: "1AAE161648DE4215", type: "xp", xp: 40 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "76AAE02263EB02CB", item: "grindless:rtg_pellet", type: "item" }]
			title: "RTG Pellets"
			x: 16.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1D931CB1451E8B5A"]
			description: [
				"The &6RTG Cell&r is a pellet behind lead with a thermopile and some fins, and it works on every world, day and night, because it burns nothing."
				"Each pellet lasts about an hour of running, and its EV power starts the first bases on Venus and Mercury."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:ev_rtg"
			id: "503863FFACA225A8"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "125CEA08554D895E", type: "xp", xp: 60 }
				{ id: "53F03289B7802D20", item: "grindless:rtg_pellet", type: "item" }
			]
			tasks: [{ id: "74D514BC27E28AF3", item: "gtceu:ev_rtg", type: "item" }]
			title: "RTG Cell"
			x: 18.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["72139ED6F4E46D37"]
			description: [
				"The &6Heavy-Water Plant&r squeezes heavy water out of Martian ice with two towers and a hydrogen sulfide loop. In the cold tower deuterium slips from the gas into the water; in the hot one it slips back out."
				"Its controller is built around a distillation tower."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:heavy_water_plant"
			id: "5A1DBDF9E739CEF2"
			rewards: [{ id: "58E46537278E0B36", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "39600F8879724225", item: "gtceu:heavy_water_plant", type: "item" }]
			title: "Heavy-Water Plant"
			x: 12.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5A1DBDF9E739CEF2", "148A0854C671B0AC"]
			description: [
				"Circuit 1 makes a concentrate from ice and steam, and circuit 2 finishes it into &6Heavy Water&r. The hydrogen sulfide sits in a hatch of its own and only circulates, so one fill lasts forever."
				"Any steam works, and the combined-cycle plant and the hot strip mill have plenty they aren't allowed to throw away."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:heavy_water_bucket"
			id: "3513B00E50D7C58B"
			rewards: [{ id: "1927F031E0113E2D", type: "xp", xp: 50 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3B84E2D84CA1A792", item: "gtceu:hydrogen_sulfide_bucket", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7A613D0C7A728F23", item: "gtceu:heavy_water_concentrate_bucket", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5AA8209BEA7FE401", item: "gtceu:heavy_water_bucket", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Heavy Water"
			x: 14.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["72139ED6F4E46D37", "3513B00E50D7C58B"]
			description: ["Heavy water slows neutrons without eating them, and on circuit 2 the same assembly gives twice the power. It comes out as &6Tritiated Heavy Water&r, and the reactor never vents it. Give it a tank."]
			icon: "gtceu:tritiated_heavy_water_bucket"
			id: "373CBFB746FCAD51"
			rewards: [{ id: "5FB7091F09100089", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "1A82047FD3D6215B", item: "gtceu:tritiated_heavy_water_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Heavy-Water Core"
			x: 14.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3513B00E50D7C58B"]
			description: ["Heavy water in the electrolyzer splits into &6Deuterium&r and oxygen, the first deuterium since Earth ran out of it. The Moon's tritium facility wants a charge, and fusion will want the rest."]
			icon: "gtceu:deuterium_bucket"
			id: "1802C3DEADA12B33"
			rewards: [{ id: "3134B8343CD4914B", type: "xp", xp: 40 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "1F57DEA61BE43132", item: "gtceu:deuterium_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Deuterium"
			x: 16.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["373CBFB746FCAD51", "79EE0C54F2D89358"]
			description: [
				"On the Moon, a cold box between two exchange columns pulls the tritium out and hands the heavy water back for the reactor. The &6Tritium Removal Facility&r is built from a cryogenic plant controller, and its deuterium charge is never drained."
				"Run it at night with every radiator open to the sky and it costs half."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:tritium_removal_facility"
			id: "32FD8F32DC829A03"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "1FB2D45849999215", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 2, id: "3D7C17422BC4EE30", item: "grindless:night_sky_radiator", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "517C82990CE93DDE", item: "gtceu:tritium_removal_facility", type: "item" }]
			title: "Tritium Removal Facility"
			x: 16.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["32FD8F32DC829A03", "1802C3DEADA12B33"]
			description: ["The only &6Tritium&r in the pack comes out of that cold box. Nothing uses it yet, but fusion will. Store every drop."]
			icon: "gtceu:tritium_bucket"
			id: "7FD8A4969E497C3A"
			rewards: [{ id: "77B41281449353DE", type: "xp", xp: 50 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "1C954386BA730522", item: "gtceu:tritium_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Tritium"
			x: 18.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["32FD8F32DC829A03", "319C39AD99B5E4A8"]
			description: [
				"While you're on the Moon, give the antenna on the far side a second EV energy hatch, the same trick the tritium facility runs on. At night, with the Mars chart calibrating the dish, it writes the &6Inner Planets Chart&r onto a data stick."
				"It's never used up, but copy it anyway: charts have a way of ending up in the wrong chest."
			]
			icon: "grindless:inner_planets_chart"
			id: "539716A235672461"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "1BFDF964AD6323E1", type: "xp", xp: 60 }
				{ count: 2, id: "15B37430C2F6B838", item: "gtceu:data_stick", type: "item" }
			]
			tasks: [{ id: "319C2A03113D6CD4", item: "grindless:inner_planets_chart", type: "item" }]
			title: "Inner Planets Chart"
			x: 18.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["539716A235672461"]
			description: [
				"Venus and Mercury want a level 3 rocket, and since GCYR averages the parts, one leftover advanced motor keeps you at level 2. The IV assembler makes the &6elite parts&r with the chart, and one trip takes two elite tanks."
				"Each suit piece gets the thermal upgrade and a heat shielding fabric in a smithing table: do all four, unless you like warm knees."
			]
			icon: "gcyr:elite_rocket_motor"
			id: "5A378E5CFD8DFF82"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "3F155B6C3573CD88", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 4, id: "5131070CAECCD5E6", item: "gcyr:heat_shielding_fabric", type: "item" }
			]
			tasks: [
				{ count: 2L, id: "59C4E8109DDA23B7", item: "gcyr:elite_fuel_tank", type: "item" }
				{ count: 6L, id: "7F07DE4F24210C8C", item: "gcyr:elite_rocket_motor", type: "item" }
				{ count: 4L, id: "501C290545582F38", item: "gcyr:space_suit_thermal_upgrade_smithing_template", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Elite Rocket, Thermal Suit"
			x: 20.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5A378E5CFD8DFF82"]
			description: [
				"Ninety bar of carbon dioxide, clouds of sulfuric acid and ground hot enough to melt lead: lovely place. Nothing burns here, so land with an RTG cell or charged batteries."
				"The cell puts out EV, which means an EV chemical reactor for the bridge seed; bring ender pearls, helium-3 and a waystone for the ride home too."
			]
			icon: "gcyr:venus_rock"
			id: "5693331C34A5A291"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "598ECBCF2FA7DA6D", type: "xp", xp: 150 }
				{ count: 3, id: "50BD5C3F1D9BFAA9", item: "grindless:empty_vein_probe", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "rsquare"
			size: 1.25d
